    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e9749f46_7e42b47c",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/trogdor/boards/arm/trogdor/trogdor_defconfig",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-06T03:35:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The watchdog implementation between Zephyr and ECOS is different.\n\nIn short, the PLATFORM_EC_WATCHDOG_PERIOD_MS is to setup the T0 timer. When the T0 timer expires, it prints the debug trace and then does a busy loop, waiting for the real watchdog trigger.\n\nThe actual watchdog timeout is PLATFORM_EC_WATCHDOG_PERIOD_MS + WDT_NPCX_DELAY_CYCLES. So it is 500ms more, not 1600ms. Since the interrupt routine does a busy loop, it actually behaves similarly.\n\nThis Zephyr implementation is different from EC-OS and some comment in Zephyr driver is wrong. I will file a bug to track. It doesn\u0027t affect this CL BTW.",
      "parentUuid": "b76502e3_5197aeaf",
